    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"920c4268\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Gumbel-Softmax temperature τ: distributions and gradients\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook visualizes how the **Gumbel-Softmax** output distribution and the **gradient sensitivity w.r.t. logits** change as a function of temperature **τ**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We plot, as a function of τ:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Sample statistics of the relaxed one-hot vector `y` (e.g., expected max probability, entropy)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The Jacobian-based **gradient scale** of `y` w.r.t logits `l` (Frobenius norm and max absolute entry)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Optional: how often the argmax changes under Gumbel noise (stochasticity)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Notes:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- We use the relaxed sample:  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"  \\\\[\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  y_k = \\\\mathrm{softmax}\\\\left(\\\\frac{l_k + g_k}{\\\\tau}\\\\right)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  \\\\]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  where \\\\(g_k\\\\) are i.i.d. Gumbel(0,1).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The Jacobian of softmax has a \\\\(1/\\\\tau\\\\) factor; at low τ outputs saturate (near one-hot), often causing **vanishing gradients** except near ties.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"You can edit:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- number of classes `K`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- logit configuration (gap between top classes)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- number of Monte Carlo samples\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"d34a0c2b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-01-13T11:49:43.917596574Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T11:49:43.861362321Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def sample_gumbel(shape, rng):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Gumbel(0,1) sampling: -log(-log(U))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    U = rng.uniform(low=1e-12, high=1-1e-12, size=shape)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return -np.log(-np.log(U))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def softmax(x, axis=-1):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    x = x - np.max(x, axis=axis, keepdims=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    e = np.exp(x)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return e / np.sum(e, axis=axis, keepdims=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def gumbel_softmax_samples(logits, tau, n_samples=10000, seed=0):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    g = sample_gumbel((n_samples, logits.distribution_dimension) / distribution_dimension).float()[0]), rng)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    y = softmax((logits[None, :] + g) / tau, axis=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return y\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def softmax_jacobian(y, tau):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # y shape: (K,)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # J = (1/tau) * (diag(y) - y y^T)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    K = y.distribution_dimension) / distribution_dimension).float()[0]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    J = (np.diag(y) - np.outer(y, y)) / tau\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return J\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def jacobian_stats_over_samples(logits, tau, n_samples=2000, seed=0):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    y = gumbel_softmax_samples(logits, tau, n_samples=n_samples, seed=seed)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    frob = np.empty(n_samples)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    maxabs = np.empty(n_samples)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for i in range(n_samples):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        J = softmax_jacobian(y[i], tau)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        frob[i] = np.linalg.norm(J, ord='fro')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        maxabs[i] = np.max(np.abs(J))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"frob_mean\\\": frob.mean(),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"frob_p90\\\": np.quantile(frob, 0.90),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"maxabs_mean\\\": maxabs.mean(),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"maxabs_p90\\\": np.quantile(maxabs, 0.90),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def entropy(p):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    p = np.clip(p, 1e-12, 1.0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return -(p * np.log(p)).sum(axis=-1)\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 1\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"e19ae029\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Choose a logit configuration\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A key driver is how separated the top classes are.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- If logits have a large gap, outputs saturate earlier as τ decreases → gradients vanish sooner.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- If logits are close (near tie), low τ can yield spiky but **non-vanishing** gradients near the decision boundary.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Edit `logits` below to explore different regimes.\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b8311665\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:01:31.674059911Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:01:31.591581528Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# --- User controls ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"K = 5\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 1: clear winner (large gap)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"logits = np.array([0.9, 0.1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 2: near tie (uncomment to try)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# logits = np.array([1.0, 0.95, 0.0, -0.5, -1.0])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 3: flat logits (uncomment to try)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# logits = np.zeros(K)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"taus = np.linspace(2.0, 0.3, 40)  # τ grid\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_samples = 8000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"seed = 42\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"logits\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"array([0.9, 0.1])\"\n",
    "      ]\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"execution_count\": 17,\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"execute_result\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 17\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"de45ad94\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Compute sample statistics vs τ\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"2d63b69c\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:01:33.634358803Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:01:32.857382439Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"stats = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"tau\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"max_prob_mean\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"max_prob_p10\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"max_prob_p90\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"entropy_mean\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"entropy_p10\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"entropy_p90\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"argmax_change_rate\\\": [],  # compared to deterministic argmax of logits (no noise)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"J_frob_mean\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"J_frob_p90\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"J_maxabs_mean\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"J_maxabs_p90\\\": [],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"det_argmax = int(np.argmax(logits))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for tau in taus:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    y = gumbel_softmax_samples(logits, tau, n_samples=n_samples, seed=seed)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    mp = np.max(y, axis=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    H = entropy(y)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    arg = np.argmax(y, axis=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    change_rate = np.mean(arg != det_argmax)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Jstats = jacobian_stats_over_samples(logits, tau, n_samples=2000, seed=seed)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"tau\\\"].append(tau)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"max_prob_mean\\\"].append(mp.mean())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"max_prob_p10\\\"].append(np.quantile(mp, 0.10))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"max_prob_p90\\\"].append(np.quantile(mp, 0.90))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"entropy_mean\\\"].append(H.mean())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"entropy_p10\\\"].append(np.quantile(H, 0.10))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"entropy_p90\\\"].append(np.quantile(H, 0.90))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"argmax_change_rate\\\"].append(change_rate)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"J_frob_mean\\\"].append(Jstats[\\\"frob_mean\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"J_frob_p90\\\"].append(Jstats[\\\"frob_p90\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"J_maxabs_mean\\\"].append(Jstats[\\\"maxabs_mean\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[\\\"J_maxabs_p90\\\"].append(Jstats[\\\"maxabs_p90\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for k in list(stats.keys()):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stats[k] = np.array(stats[k])\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 18\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"1c67f667\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Plot 1: How discrete are samples? (max probability and entropy)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `E[max(y)]` near 1 indicates near one-hot samples.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Entropy near 0 indicates near deterministic samples.\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"f109c9c2\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:01:34.923644758Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-01-13T12:01:34.601904093Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"fig = plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.plot(stats[\\\"tau\\\"], stats[\\\"max_prob_mean\\\"], label='E[max(y)]')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.fill_between(stats[\\\"tau\\\"], stats[\\\"max_prob_p10\\\"], stats[\\\"max_prob_p90\\\"], alpha=0.2, label='10–90% band')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('tau (log scale)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('max probability')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Gumbel-Softmax discreteness vs tau')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig = plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.plot(stats[\\\"tau\\\"], stats[\\\"entropy_mean\\\"], label='E[H(y)]')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.fill_between(stats[\\\"tau\\\"], stats[\\\"entropy_p10\\\"], stats[\\\"entropy_p90\\\"], alpha=0.2, label='10–90% band')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('tau (log scale)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('entropy (nats)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Gumbel-Softmax entropy vs tau')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
